    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "About this pipeline",
      "description": "Static notes for whoever opens this dashboard.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 13
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### What this pipeline does\n**loghub_etl** turns each day's Spark/HDFS log drop into hourly event counts:\n`bronze_ingest \u2192 silver_parse \u2192 quality_checks \u2192 gold_aggregate \u2192 record_run`\n\n- **Schedule:** daily 05:00 UTC (paused in dev) \u00b7 gold due 06:00 UTC\n- **Owner:** data-platform-team (on-call)\n- **Alerts:** email on failure; warning if a run takes > 15 min\n- **Data:** `workspace.pipeline_demo` \u00b7 landing volume `raw_logs/<source>/<date>/`\n\n### How to read this dashboard\nGreen tiles = healthy. A red **Last run** tile or any **Failed runs** means an incident.\nOpen the run from **Latest runs** (click the run id), check which **task** failed,\nthen use the matching runbook below.\n\n### Runbooks by failed task\n| Task | Usual cause | Runbook |\n|---|---|---|\n| bronze_ingest | file never arrived / wrong path | missing-input-data |\n| silver_parse | new or changed columns | schema-change |\n| quality_checks | bad timestamps, empty or misdated batch | data-quality-breach |\n| gold_aggregate | no write permission / out of memory | access-and-permissions \u00b7 resource-exhaustion |\n"
      }
    },
